# Vercel deploys ONLY the static dashboard (index.html, src/) and the Node
# serverless API routes (api/*.js). Everything below powers the Render-hosted
# Sentinel ML service and local ML tooling — it must NOT be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Why this file exists:
# When the Sentinel inference moved off Vercel to Render, api/inference.py was
# removed but its Python footprint stayed at the repo root (.python-version, a
# heavy requirements.txt, root *.py scripts, __pycache__). Vercel's zero-config
# build inspects the root, saw those Python signals, and stopped naturally
# emitting the Node functions under api/ — so /api/weather/current returned 404.
# Excluding the Python/ML footprint lets zero-config expose api/weather/current.js
# again. No ML code is modified; these files simply are not part of the Vercel build.

# --- Python runtime / build-detection triggers at repo root ---
.python-version
requirements.txt
*.py
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# --- ML pipeline, Sentinel API service, model artifacts, tests, data ---
# (used by Render + local ML only; not needed by the frontend or Node API)
ml/
sentinel_api/
models/
tests/
data/
